@startuml
' How a page's metadata ends up in the document head.
'
' The detail worth noticing: Filament renders its <head> render hooks outside
' the Livewire component's own scope, so the page cannot simply be asked for its
' metadata at that point. The page publishes it from a Livewire lifecycle hook
' instead, and the render hook reads it back from the registry.

title How metadata reaches the document head

skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  LifeLineBorderColor #94a3b8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #f8fafc
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #ffffff
  ActorBorderColor #475569
  ActorBackgroundColor #ffffff
}
autonumber

actor Visitor
participant "Filament" as Filament
participant "About\n(Page + HasSeoMetadata)" as Page
participant "SeoRegistry\n(scoped binding)" as Registry
participant "FilamentSeoPlugin" as Plugin
participant "MetaTags" as MetaTags

Visitor -> Filament : GET /about
activate Filament

Filament -> Page : mount, then boot Livewire
activate Page

Page -> Page : bootedHasSeoMetadata()
Page -> Page : getSeoData()
note right of Page
  Reads the page's own
  seoTitle / seoDescription
  properties, and falls back to
  the record's getSeoData()
  when the page renders one.
end note
Page -> Registry : set(SeoData)
deactivate Page

Filament -> Plugin : HEAD_END render hook
activate Plugin

Plugin -> Registry : get()
Registry --> Plugin : SeoData, or null
deactivate Registry

Plugin -> Plugin : page data ?? panel data
Plugin -> Plugin : layer site name and canonical underneath
Plugin -> MetaTags : render(SeoData, withTitle)
MetaTags --> Plugin : description, robots, canonical,\nog:*, twitter:*
Plugin --> Filament : markup
deactivate Plugin

Filament --> Visitor : the document head
deactivate Filament

@enduml
